WEBVTT

00:01.280 --> 00:04.760
Kono omoi wo keshite shimau niwa

00:04.760 --> 00:07.100
mada jinsei nagai dsho?

00:08.080 --> 00:13.540
Yarinokoshite'ru koto
yarinaoshite mitai kara

00:23.300 --> 00:29.540
Yume no tsuzuki oikakete ita hazu na no ni

00:29.860 --> 00:35.880
Magarikunetta
hosoi michi hito ni tsumazuku

00:35.880 --> 00:42.800
Ano koro mitai ni tte modoritai wake ja nai ni
Nakushite kita sora wo sagashite'ru

00:42.800 --> 00:44.420
Wakatte kuremasu you ni

00:44.420 --> 00:49.580
Gisei ni natta you na
kanashii kao wa yamete yo

00:49.580 --> 00:53.040
Tsumi no saigo wa namida ja nai yo
Zutto kurushiku seotte'ku n da

00:53.040 --> 00:56.420
Deguchi mienai kanjou meiro ni
dare wo matte'ru no?

00:56.420 --> 01:00.000
Shiroi nooto ni tsuzutta you ni
motto sunao ni hakidashitai yo

01:00.000 --> 01:03.140
Nani kar nogaretai n da
genjitsu tte yatsu?

01:03.140 --> 01:09.840
Kanaeru tame ni ikite'ru n datte
Sakebitaku naru yo Kikoete imasu ka?

01:09.860 --> 01:14.940
Bunai n nante yatte'rarenai kara

01:14.980 --> 01:16.820
...kaeru basho mo nai no

01:16.820 --> 01:20.120
Yasashisa niwa itsumo kansha shite'ru

01:20.120 --> 01:23.600
Dakara tsuyoku naritai
(I'm on the way)

01:23.600 --> 01:27.260
Natsukashiku naru
konna itami mo kangei jan

01:27.260 --> 01:30.780

01:33.960 --> 01:36.800
In search of the dark secrets
of the Philosopher's Stone,

01:36.800 --> 01:40.800
Ed and Al break into the
supposedly deserted Fifth Laboratory.

01:40.800 --> 01:43.760
There they encounter
two guards who, like Al,

01:43.770 --> 01:46.400
have had their souls
bonded to suits of armor.

01:47.050 --> 01:51.960
In the course of their fight, Al's
opponent, 66, plants suspicions in his mind.

01:52.360 --> 01:55.800
Al begins to wonder if he is a
counterfeit soul created by Ed,

01:55.800 --> 01:59.800
and bonded to a suit of armor to
become the older boy's biddable puppet.

02:05.540 --> 02:07.200
ROSS: Looks like you can sit up now, huh?

02:07.380 --> 02:09.520
[CRICKETS CHIRPING]

02:09.620 --> 02:11.480
What happened with the Fifth Laboratory?

02:11.520 --> 02:12.800
Well, it, um...

02:13.040 --> 02:16.340
Somebody blew up the building and
there's nothing left of it now but rubble.

02:16.360 --> 02:18.840
Damn it!
You mean they wiped out everything?

02:20.600 --> 02:21.800
That didn't feel good.

02:22.500 --> 02:24.800
This isn't fair...

02:25.240 --> 02:27.800
Do you know how close I
was to finding out the truth?

02:28.100 --> 02:31.100
This is no time for me to
be lying around in a hospital.

02:31.680 --> 02:32.420
BOTH: Hm.

02:33.820 --> 02:35.400
BOTH: Fullmetal Alchemist, sir!

02:35.460 --> 02:36.060
Hm?

02:36.200 --> 02:38.480
We do apologize in advance for this!

02:38.660 --> 02:39.380
Huh?

02:40.800 --> 02:41.800
[SMACK]

02:46.850 --> 02:48.800
You acted like a selfish child.

02:48.900 --> 02:51.800
You only escaped with your
life because you were lucky.

02:53.250 --> 02:55.800
You don't have to do everything
all on your own, you know.

02:56.050 --> 02:57.800
You can lean on other people.

03:00.500 --> 03:01.800
Like us.

03:02.150 --> 03:04.800
Not all adults are the enemy.
You can trust us.

03:09.480 --> 03:10.700
BOTH: That's all!

03:11.020 --> 03:13.540
Please forgive our abusive
words and conduct, sir!

03:13.640 --> 03:15.240
It will not happen again!

03:15.300 --> 03:15.860
Uh...

03:17.400 --> 03:18.800
No, you're right.

03:19.420 --> 03:21.080
I should be apologizing.

03:22.050 --> 03:24.800
My punishment...
for slapping you.

03:24.940 --> 03:25.800
Huh?

03:25.800 --> 03:27.240
Nothing, I had it coming.

03:27.280 --> 03:28.780
[RELIEVED SOUNDS]

03:28.800 --> 03:30.800
What's got you two so scared of me?

03:30.900 --> 03:35.000
- State-certified alchemists carry a military rank equivalent to that of a Major.
- Mm-hmm.

03:35.120 --> 03:36.380
Don't worry about it.

03:36.400 --> 03:39.360
I didn't get my certification
so people would kiss up to me.

03:39.640 --> 03:42.440
You don't have to talk to me
like I'm a high-ranking officer.

03:42.480 --> 03:43.800
Really? Oh!

03:43.830 --> 03:46.220
Ah, I guess we were
scared of the brat for nothing.

03:46.520 --> 03:48.100
They adjust quickly...

03:48.860 --> 03:51.300
Um, where's Al? I haven't seen him.

03:51.460 --> 03:53.480
Alphonse got his own lecture earlier.

03:53.520 --> 03:56.100
But I was the one who did the slapping.

03:56.120 --> 03:57.720
[PAINED LAUGHTER]

03:59.420 --> 04:00.640
I almost forgot.

04:00.660 --> 04:03.840
I have an even less pleasant
lecture in store for me today.

04:08.200 --> 04:08.960
[PHONE RINGING]

04:09.180 --> 04:11.680
Hello? Rockbell Prosthetic Glam Outfitters.

04:13.460 --> 04:14.380
Oh, Ed.

04:14.580 --> 04:17.340
Since when do you ever bother to call us, is something wrong?

04:17.460 --> 04:18.200
Yeah...

04:18.700 --> 04:19.800
Here's the deal.

04:20.040 --> 04:24.640
I hate to ask you, but...do you think you
could make a service call out to Central for me?

04:24.780 --> 04:25.800
A service call?

04:25.820 --> 04:26.600
Yeah.

04:26.850 --> 04:28.520
My right arm's messed up again.

04:28.680 --> 04:30.860
I can move the fingers,
but that's about it.

04:30.920 --> 04:32.120
I can't lift the arm at all.

04:32.140 --> 04:32.800
[GASPS]

04:36.440 --> 04:37.880
[NERVOUS LAUGH]

04:37.960 --> 04:40.180
- Yeah, that sounds about right.
- Huh?

04:40.220 --> 04:41.800
Nothing! Just talking to myself.

04:42.060 --> 04:44.380
So, what were you doing
when the arm stopped working?

04:45.240 --> 04:46.800
Uh... [GULPS]

04:48.260 --> 04:49.700
I was in a really rough fight.

04:49.740 --> 04:51.500
You did it again, moron!

04:51.560 --> 04:55.880
How could you treat my precious automail like that, Alchemy Freak?!

04:59.440 --> 05:01.300
Uh, are you there?

05:01.900 --> 05:03.640
Hello, Winry.

05:03.800 --> 05:05.420
Guess I've got no choice.

05:05.480 --> 05:06.600
Tell me how to get there.

05:08.440 --> 05:10.420
ED: You're sure in a good mood today.

05:10.460 --> 05:13.800
I thought you were going to—you know what? Never mind. Forget it.

05:13.800 --> 05:14.800
Yeah.

05:14.800 --> 05:15.800
Yep.

05:16.060 --> 05:17.700
Sorry again, and thanks.

05:17.780 --> 05:18.500
Right.

05:18.920 --> 05:19.820
Goodbye.

05:20.960 --> 05:21.840
[EXHALES]

05:21.860 --> 05:23.120
Aw, was that your girlfriend?

05:23.140 --> 05:25.680
My girlfriend?! No way!

05:26.780 --> 05:28.560
It's nothing to be embarrassed about.

05:28.600 --> 05:31.000
When I was your age, I had a
different girlfriend every week.

05:31.180 --> 05:31.720
Hmm?

05:31.780 --> 05:34.400
What are you doing sitting
there in the dark by yourself?

05:35.240 --> 05:35.860
Hey.

05:36.240 --> 05:37.020
Hey,  Al.

05:37.520 --> 05:38.540
Brother.

05:38.650 --> 05:40.820
You know you can come to the room, right?

05:46.800 --> 05:48.760
I'll be there in a little while.

05:49.400 --> 05:50.800
You go on ahead.

05:50.800 --> 05:51.800
Okay.

05:59.200 --> 06:02.960
[SOFT, MECHANICAL FOOTSTEPS]

06:11.140 --> 06:12.460
[GIGGLE]

06:12.600 --> 06:13.560
Bye!

06:18.960 --> 06:23.580
Are you sure you're not a puppet
created by your so-called brother?

06:29.500 --> 06:31.800
[BELLS RINGING]

06:31.800 --> 06:34.400
Ugh, that left me really sore.

06:34.420 --> 06:37.320
I don't understand how Ed
and Al can ride on these things.

06:40.240 --> 06:42.040
Ed said to look near the west exit.

06:42.060 --> 06:45.560
There'd be someone familiar there
who I'd recognize right away.

06:46.820 --> 06:49.160
Hello, Major Armstrong, it's Winry!

06:51.080 --> 06:53.600
Hello, Miss Winry. Did you have a pleasant trip?

06:55.260 --> 06:57.320
Where are those stupid Elric brothers?

06:57.440 --> 06:58.200
[GULPS]

06:58.850 --> 07:00.680
Well, you see...

07:01.000 --> 07:01.800
Hmm?

07:01.900 --> 07:05.760
[INDISCERNIBLE]

07:06.300 --> 07:08.800
The hospital? What happened?!

07:11.640 --> 07:13.560
ED: Well, that didn't take long.

07:13.920 --> 07:17.300
You're gonna charge me an
express service fee now, aren't you?

07:18.740 --> 07:21.100
No, I... I won't
charge you for this.

07:21.100 --> 07:23.560
I didn't do a good enough job on your automail last time.

07:25.150 --> 07:26.800
And now you're badly injured.

07:30.780 --> 07:33.520
It's not your fault! You can't blame yourself for this!

07:33.840 --> 07:35.960
I broke it because I was being reckless!

07:36.060 --> 07:39.720
Your repairs were flawless as ever! This was all my fault!

07:40.080 --> 07:41.620
WINRY: He has no idea...

07:41.720 --> 07:44.160
He never noticed that I
forgot to put in that screw.

07:44.220 --> 07:46.640
Besides, if my arm hadn't
broken when it did, I would have

07:46.680 --> 07:49.100
kept fighting and then I would
have been hurt even worse!

07:49.250 --> 07:50.800
So don't worry about it, okay?

07:50.800 --> 07:51.800
Okay?

07:51.900 --> 07:53.800
WINRY: So it turned out all right?

07:54.120 --> 07:55.540
[LAUGHS]

07:55.800 --> 07:58.380
Well, then, let's go ahead and get right down to business, shall we?

07:58.440 --> 08:01.060
I'll have to charge you the
usual rush order fee, of course.

08:01.100 --> 08:01.800
Huh?

08:01.800 --> 08:02.800
Hmm?

08:05.100 --> 08:06.540
You didn't drink your milk.

08:08.240 --> 08:09.500
Why should I?

08:09.700 --> 08:10.560
I hate it.

08:10.600 --> 08:14.760
You're going to be small and stunted
forever if you keep using that stupid excuse!

08:14.800 --> 08:15.740
Shut up!

08:15.800 --> 08:17.980
I don't have to drink it if I don't wanna!

08:18.020 --> 08:20.840
You sound like a spoiled little brat, Edward Elric!

08:22.220 --> 08:23.980
ROSS: Every growing boy needs his milk.

08:24.000 --> 08:26.040
BROSH: Yeah, you want the girls to like ya, don't you?

08:27.850 --> 08:30.800
- Was that Al?
- Hmm?

08:36.880 --> 08:37.840
ED: I don't get it.

08:37.860 --> 08:39.520
Al's been acting really weird lately.

08:40.820 --> 08:42.040
WINRY: Weird how?

08:45.240 --> 08:47.240
Just seems like something's
been bothering him.

09:01.100 --> 09:05.300
Are you sure you're not a puppet
created by your so-called brother?

09:05.300 --> 09:06.800
Just accept it.

09:06.860 --> 09:08.060
You'll feel better.

09:08.060 --> 09:09.220
[MIRROR CRACKS]

09:16.280 --> 09:18.020
WINRY: Okay! You're all set.

09:18.800 --> 09:20.380
[GROANS] Well done!

09:20.440 --> 09:22.760
Ah, it feels good to have it back.

09:22.900 --> 09:24.620
Wow, thanks a lot.

09:24.880 --> 09:26.460
Sure, no problem.

09:26.460 --> 09:27.260
[DOOR OPENS]
Hm?

09:27.380 --> 09:28.900
Yo, Ed, my boy!

09:29.000 --> 09:33.000
Is it true you brought a pretty blonde
girl into your room to service you?

09:34.100 --> 09:36.940
She's my automail mechanic, that's all! Nothing more!

09:37.020 --> 09:38.220
Oh, I see.

09:38.360 --> 09:39.540
You've seduced your mechanic, have you?

09:39.620 --> 09:40.760
[SCREAMS]

09:40.760 --> 09:44.000
That isn't what I said at all! Were you even listening to me?!

09:44.780 --> 09:47.120
Maes Hughes, I'm pleased
to meet you, young lady.

09:47.140 --> 09:49.020
You too, I'm Winry Rockbell.

09:49.220 --> 09:50.460
Nice to see you, Hughes.

09:50.520 --> 09:52.460
But don't you have work to do?

09:52.480 --> 09:53.960
Nope, it's all under control.

09:54.180 --> 09:56.060
I gave Sheska some overtime.

09:56.760 --> 09:58.160
ED: You're a real jerk, aren't you?

09:58.180 --> 10:00.160
Oh, yeah, and I think you'll be happy to know...

10:00.220 --> 10:03.840
I just found out you and Al shouldn't need to be kept
under guard for too much longer.

10:03.900 --> 10:05.800
ED: Great!
WINRY: What'd you say?

10:06.060 --> 10:07.500
Hold on just a second!

10:07.540 --> 10:10.400
How much trouble have you
gotten yourself into this time?

10:11.180 --> 10:13.800
Uh, well, you see, it's...

10:15.980 --> 10:18.420
Well, it's nothing that concerns you.

10:26.300 --> 10:27.140
Of course not.

10:27.180 --> 10:28.900
I don't know why I bother to try.

10:28.920 --> 10:30.560
It's not like you'll talk to me anyway.

10:32.780 --> 10:34.220
Fine, I'll see you tomorrow.

10:35.000 --> 10:38.340
I have to go and see if I
can find some place to stay tonight.

10:38.420 --> 10:41.580
Come on, no need for that. Why don't you spend the night at my place?

10:41.900 --> 10:42.880
Really?

10:42.900 --> 10:43.720
Yes, of course.

10:43.740 --> 10:46.200
My wife and daughter will
be delighted to have you.

10:46.200 --> 10:48.540
- Oh no, I—
- It's settled. Come on, come on.

10:49.140 --> 10:50.320
Here, let me take that.

10:50.320 --> 10:52.200
Oh, I've got it! Let's go!

10:52.240 --> 10:54.560
- Do you really have to drag me?
- [LAUGHING]

10:58.440 --> 11:01.660
[POPPING]
[LAUGHTER]

11:01.720 --> 11:03.960
Happy birthday, Elicia!

11:05.780 --> 11:07.480
[CHEERING]

11:07.520 --> 11:11.600
Um, you don't mind me asking, Mr. Hughes, what is this all about?

11:11.640 --> 11:13.800
I'm so glad you asked that, Miss Winry.

11:14.100 --> 11:17.120
Today happens to be my
darling little Elicia's birthday!

11:17.240 --> 11:18.580
Yeah, my birthday!

11:18.950 --> 11:20.800
[LAUGHING]

11:21.080 --> 11:23.560
That's exciting.
How old are you now, Elicia?

11:23.700 --> 11:24.700
I'm two!

11:26.820 --> 11:28.480
No, I'm three!

11:29.420 --> 11:32.040
Oh how adorable!

11:32.400 --> 11:34.180
Fullmetal Alchemist.

11:35.500 --> 11:37.260
Fullmetal Alchemist

11:40.740 --> 11:43.760
I've known the Elrics for about
as long as I can remember.

11:43.840 --> 11:46.280
We grew up together.
They're like my brothers.

11:46.360 --> 11:49.700
And I'm sure knowing those two,
they must give you plenty to worry about.

11:49.720 --> 11:51.480
That's an understatement.

11:51.500 --> 11:56.260
When they finally came back for a visit, it
was because Ed's arm was all busted up.

11:59.500 --> 12:02.800
And now he calls me out here because
he's been seriously injured again.

12:03.740 --> 12:05.800
Something's bothering Al, too.

12:07.280 --> 12:09.170
They keep their mouths shut, though.

12:09.500 --> 12:11.460
They don't ever tell me what's going on.

12:11.940 --> 12:14.800
It's just like when they left
Resembool for the first time.

12:16.160 --> 12:17.930
HUGHES: Maybe nothing needed to be said.

12:20.300 --> 12:21.800
You know these boys, Winry.

12:21.960 --> 12:25.040
It's possible they thought you'd
understand without them saying anything.

12:28.520 --> 12:29.500
Maybe.

12:29.940 --> 12:32.980
But there are some things
that I actually need to be told.

12:34.620 --> 12:36.440
Just what am I going to do with you?

12:38.200 --> 12:41.800
In general, men prefer to let their
actions speak instead of words.

12:42.260 --> 12:44.800
When they're in pain, they don't
want to burden anyone with it.

12:45.000 --> 12:46.320
Not if they can help it.

12:47.060 --> 12:49.080
They don't want anyone to worry about them.

12:49.460 --> 12:50.800
That's how they are.

12:53.780 --> 12:56.980
Even so, there may come a
time when they'll ask for your help.

12:58.200 --> 13:01.380
And when they do, I know
that you'll be there for them.

13:02.500 --> 13:03.800
Isn't that enough?

13:06.450 --> 13:09.260
Elicia, we wanna play! Let's go!

13:09.400 --> 13:10.940
Will you put me down now?

13:10.980 --> 13:12.800
WINRY: Okay, down you go.

13:13.640 --> 13:14.940
Hey, you get away from her!

13:14.980 --> 13:16.800
Elicia wants to play with me, not you!

13:17.660 --> 13:20.440
She's quite the heartbreaker
already, isn't she?

13:20.880 --> 13:22.440
[GUN COCKING]

13:22.960 --> 13:24.640
Listen up, boys.

13:24.760 --> 13:27.800
You try anything with my
daughter, and you will answer to me.

13:28.120 --> 13:29.800
Your actions speak too loudly!

13:35.020 --> 13:36.800
GRACIA: Are you sure you have to go?

13:36.850 --> 13:39.800
You're more than welcome to stay
with us for as long as you're in town.

13:40.140 --> 13:42.680
I don't want to put you out
more than I have already.

13:45.180 --> 13:47.520
Elicia's gotten very attached to you.

13:47.520 --> 13:48.940
[LAUGHS]

13:48.940 --> 13:51.800
Well, would you look at that!
The two of you could be sisters.

13:52.100 --> 13:56.800
Sissy! Be safe, okay?
And come back and visit me real soon!

13:57.400 --> 13:59.800
It's settled.
You're staying with us again tonight.

14:01.660 --> 14:03.660
[BOTH GIGGLING]

14:03.660 --> 14:06.480
It looks like I found
myself a little sister.

14:13.040 --> 14:16.800
So we meet again, you little bastard.
I'm not gonna drink you.

14:18.400 --> 14:21.800
Brother, you have a living
body that needs nourishment.

14:22.530 --> 14:23.800
You have to drink it.

14:26.040 --> 14:27.800
I don't have to if I don't want to.

14:28.500 --> 14:30.800
It may not look like it, but I have grown some.

14:31.060 --> 14:33.240
But everyone still calls me a pipsqueak.

14:34.800 --> 14:36.380
I wish I was like you, Al.

14:38.000 --> 14:39.800
You've got such a big body now.

14:42.640 --> 14:46.480
It's not like I asked
for this body, brother!

14:48.000 --> 14:52.340
Sorry. You're right.
It's my fault that it happened.

14:53.100 --> 14:57.300
But I'll make it right. I'll get you
back into your real body. You'll see, Al.

14:57.300 --> 15:00.020
AL: That's what you always say,
but you don't know that for sure!

15:00.040 --> 15:03.800
L-look, I promise I'm gonna get you back.
Believe me, Al. I'll do it.

15:03.850 --> 15:04.900
Believe you?

15:04.920 --> 15:08.800
How am I supposed to believe
anything when I'm stuck in this body?

15:09.100 --> 15:11.240
What should I believe in? My memories?

15:11.340 --> 15:15.800
Memories are just scraps of information that
can be made up as easily as anything else.

15:15.960 --> 15:18.260
Al, what are you talking about?

15:18.280 --> 15:21.800
Do you remember when you said there
was something you were afraid to tell me?

15:22.280 --> 15:25.500
I think...
I think I might know what it was.

15:26.280 --> 15:31.800
Maybe you wanted to say that my soul and my memories
are really artificial constructions you created!

15:34.800 --> 15:40.800
You... Winry and Granny... You've
been lying to me all along, haven't you?

15:40.800 --> 15:43.220
What do you have to
say for yourself, brother?

15:46.480 --> 15:50.260
ED: Is that what you really think?
Have you believed that all this time?

15:50.300 --> 15:51.160
[GASP]

15:53.480 --> 15:57.180
So, are you finished?
Or is there more you wanted to say?

16:03.100 --> 16:03.800
Okay.

16:14.500 --> 16:15.500
Don't go.

16:16.400 --> 16:17.380
Ed!

16:20.320 --> 16:21.580
WINRY: Al, you...

16:22.020 --> 16:24.240
...Moron!

16:24.260 --> 16:25.280
[CLANG]

16:25.280 --> 16:26.780
ALL: Ah!

16:26.780 --> 16:29.320
Where did that come from?!

16:29.800 --> 16:31.800
[PANTING]

16:34.280 --> 16:36.420
[GASPS] Winry?!

16:36.480 --> 16:37.440
You idiot!

16:37.440 --> 16:38.520
[CLANG]

16:38.520 --> 16:40.580
You have no idea how Ed feels!

16:41.560 --> 16:44.600
Do you know what he was
so afraid to talk to you about?

16:45.180 --> 16:49.760
He wants to know if you blame him
for what happened to your body, Al!

16:51.520 --> 16:55.020
It's all my fault.
Al lost his body and it's all my fault.

16:55.060 --> 16:58.480
He can't eat anymore, he can't
sleep, he can't feel cold or warm.

16:58.540 --> 17:02.800
He's my little brother and I'm supposed to protect him
and I did this and—[SOBBING]

17:02.950 --> 17:04.800
How could he ever forgive me?

17:04.860 --> 17:07.700
Al isn't the type of boy who would resent you for this.

17:07.780 --> 17:09.740
Just ask him and I'm sure you'll see.

17:09.800 --> 17:12.480
No. I'm... I'm too afraid.

17:12.940 --> 17:15.180
I'm too scared of what he'll say.

17:15.360 --> 17:17.540
[CLANGING]

17:17.560 --> 17:23.460
And then... you idiot! You said that!

17:25.040 --> 17:27.140
Whoever'd do something like that?

17:27.540 --> 17:32.120
Who would be prepared to risk his own
life to create a fake brother?

17:33.280 --> 17:35.640
Don't you get it? [SNIFFLES]

17:35.660 --> 17:39.800
All the two of you have left... is each other.

17:41.000 --> 17:44.800
Now! Go get your brother!

17:46.960 --> 17:48.960
- Start running!
- Right!

18:04.640 --> 18:06.340
- Bro—
- You know something, Al?

18:06.400 --> 18:09.800
We haven't had a good fight in a while.
I'm starting to get flabby.

18:09.800 --> 18:10.800
Huh?

18:19.360 --> 18:21.800
Huh? Hey!

18:23.400 --> 18:24.800
Hold on, brother!

18:25.860 --> 18:27.100
Stop!

18:28.720 --> 18:31.800
Your wounds haven't healed enough for this!

18:38.280 --> 18:42.500
I beat you! The first time I ever won!

18:44.900 --> 18:47.140
It wasn't a fair fight, brother.

18:47.180 --> 18:50.240
Don't give me that.
A win is a win and you know it, Al.

18:51.500 --> 18:55.140
We've always fought like this.
Ever since we were really little.

18:56.350 --> 19:00.180
Now that I think about it, we've fought
over some really stupid things, haven't we?

19:00.400 --> 19:03.740
Definitely. Like who would
get the top and bottom bunks.

19:03.800 --> 19:04.800
Yeah.

19:05.020 --> 19:07.000
AL: We fought over candy a lot too, huh?

19:07.000 --> 19:08.720
ED: And that toy, you remember?

19:08.880 --> 19:12.080
AL: I won that one.
And when we played in the rain river too.

19:12.080 --> 19:14.800
ED: Oh yeah. You shoved me into the water.

19:14.950 --> 19:16.800
AL: And that fight we had during our training?

19:16.800 --> 19:19.310
ED: Teacher said we were
being too loud, then she beat

19:19.330 --> 19:21.800
us up herself. Why don't
we call that one a draw?

19:21.800 --> 19:25.120
AL: We even fought over which one
of us would marry Winry someday.

19:25.140 --> 19:27.040
ED: What?! I don't remember that one.

19:27.060 --> 19:29.820
AL: I won the fight, but she shot me down.

19:29.920 --> 19:31.600
ED: Oh...did she?

19:40.180 --> 19:42.640
You're telling me that all
those memories are lies?

19:42.980 --> 19:43.900
AL: Sorry.

19:44.240 --> 19:47.980
ED: And your determination to be whole again
to get your body back no matter what...

19:48.230 --> 19:49.600
That's a lie too?

19:50.440 --> 19:52.800
AL: No, it's not a lie.
ED: That's Right

19:53.620 --> 19:55.360
We're in this together, all the way.

19:55.480 --> 19:58.120
And forget that, we're
gonna keep pushing forward.

19:58.620 --> 20:03.060
We'll make ourselves stronger, faster,
and better until we get our bodies back.

20:03.380 --> 20:05.100
[AL CHUCKLES] And the milk?

20:05.200 --> 20:08.800
ED: Milk?! Fine. I'll drink...a little.

20:08.940 --> 20:10.940
[BOTH LAUGHING]

20:10.940 --> 20:12.800
ED: Whatever it takes, brother.
AL: Mm!

20:14.740 --> 20:16.040
Mr. Hughes?

20:16.640 --> 20:20.800
Maybe you don't have to hear something out loud,
but it sure is helpful sometimes.

20:22.660 --> 20:24.740
I guess it is.

20:41.120 --> 20:42.800
My brother...

20:43.600 --> 20:44.960
Master...

20:45.040 --> 20:47.080
They're gone. All gone.

20:47.160 --> 20:48.680
Hey!

20:49.580 --> 20:52.080
You don't look like an Ishvalan.
Who are you?

20:52.380 --> 20:56.160
KIMBLEE: Oh my, where are my manners?
I should have introduced myself.

20:56.660 --> 20:59.220
I'm a State Alchemist
sent here by the military.

20:59.560 --> 21:02.380
I've been sent to
exterminate this sector.

21:09.680 --> 21:11.780
Hey, you're awake!

21:12.800 --> 21:13.680
Where am I?

21:13.740 --> 21:17.480
In a slum outside of East City.
You're among friends now.

21:18.800 --> 21:21.080
Who are you? You, old man.

21:21.560 --> 21:24.760
Me? Why, I'm a man of
Ishvala, just as you are, son.

21:24.880 --> 21:29.080
There's nothing to worry about here.
I won't sell out one of my own.

21:29.200 --> 21:33.060
Are we the only ones here?
Are there other Ishvalan survivors?

21:33.140 --> 21:35.220
Yes, indeed there are.

21:35.380 --> 21:39.620
A run-down slum such as this may
bear no resemblance to our ancestral home,

21:39.780 --> 21:42.880
But you know what they
say, the world is God's bosom.

21:42.980 --> 21:46.800
Our great, loving God Ishvala. Am I right? [CHUCKLES]

21:47.780 --> 21:49.540
Yes, you certainly are.

21:50.200 --> 21:52.080
You can't, you're not ready!

21:52.100 --> 21:55.400
We found you
floating in the sewers. You were hurt bad.

22:03.840 --> 22:07.560
Boy, my right arm.
Did I lose it or is it still with me?

22:07.660 --> 22:10.040
Yeah, it's still there, mister.
It should be fine.

22:12.920 --> 22:15.920
Your tattoo...it's really amazing.

22:17.800 --> 22:24.800
Yes, it's important to me.
A precious gift from my family.

22:28.380 --> 22:34.200
Ano hi mita sora akaneiro no sora o

22:34.280 --> 22:39.500
nee kimi wa oboete imasu ka

22:39.560 --> 22:45.260
Yakusoku chigiri shoka
no kaze ga tsutsumu

22:45.520 --> 22:50.400
futari yorisotta

22:53.480 --> 22:58.660
Muri na egao no ura

22:58.660 --> 23:04.040
nobita kage o kakumau

23:04.080 --> 23:13.420
Dakara kizukanu furi saisei o erabu

23:15.500 --> 23:22.640
Table no ue no furuenai shirase machitsuzukete

23:26.060 --> 23:31.480
kuuhaku no yoru o kuru hazu no nai asa mo

23:31.480 --> 23:35.780
zenbu wakatte'tan da

23:35.860 --> 23:41.340
Ano hi mita sora akaneiro no sora o

23:41.340 --> 23:46.540
nee itsuka omoidasu deshou

23:46.540 --> 23:51.980
Hatasenakatta yakusoku o idaite

23:52.220 --> 23:57.040
futari arukidasu

23:59.940 --> 24:02.420
A good friend became
a comrade-in-arms,

24:02.600 --> 24:05.460
and over time, his presence was taken for granted.

24:06.700 --> 24:10.920
Although the future they once dreamed of
became bleaker than they had ever imagined,

24:11.040 --> 24:15.120
this good friend was always there
by his side, where he belonged.

24:15.720 --> 24:18.980
Next time on Fullmetal Alchemist: Brotherhood

24:19.820 --> 24:22.980
Episode 10: Separate Destinations.

24:23.700 --> 24:28.380
A friend whose presence comes as naturally
as breathing can never be replaced.
